.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp

# Personal data silo — never committed. See private.example/README.md.
/private/

# Wrangler local cache/build output - never commit. Unanchored so it catches
# any depth, not just the two dirs that have a wrangler.toml today: a stray
# worker/.wrangler/ survived the server/ rename and sat untracked in every
# git status, holding a cached wrangler-account.json.
.wrangler/

# npm install output, if anyone runs it locally (server/package.json and
# client/package.json are mainly for the Deploy to Cloudflare button, which
# installs its own copy)
node_modules/
# The lockfile that install writes goes with it. Committing one would pin
# wrangler for every installer who forks this - off a version that only ever
# got there because somebody ran `npm install` locally to test a migration -
# and the Deploy button resolves its own copy regardless. Unanchored, same
# reason as .wrangler/ above: it appears next to whichever package.json was
# installed, and both of them can be.
package-lock.json

# This installer's own API URL - treated like private/ data (see
# client/public/local-config.example.js). Never commit a real deployment's
# URL into the tracked template that other installers fork.
client/public/local-config.js

# Wrangler local dev secrets (ADMIN_TOKEN etc.) - never commit
server/.dev.vars
client/.dev.vars
